# Nougat extraction — stub

**Not run.** Reason: the source PDF (`source/paper.pdf`, Abolfath/Grosshans/Mohan 2020, Med Phys 47(12)) was produced by pdfTeX 1.40.21 with a native LaTeX text layer. `pdftotext -layout` produced a clean 729-line text extraction (`ocr/paper.txt`) with no character-recognition errors, so a Nougat pass would add no value for downstream analysis — the equations, tables, and figure captions are already textually correct in the pdftotext output, and the paper's headline numeric claims (e.g. "N2 at UHDR is approximately twice N2 at CDR", Fig 7 caption) were parsed directly from that extraction.

If a Nougat rerun is later required (e.g. for equation-level LaTeX round-tripping of Eqs 1–9), the recommended invocation is:

```
nougat source/paper.pdf --model 0.1.0-base --out extraction/nougat_raw.mmd
```

on a GPU host (Nougat is inference-heavy on CPU). Expected wall-time on a single A100 is ~30 s for an 11-page article.

## What is available now
- `ocr/paper.txt` — 729 lines, pdftotext -layout output. Sufficient for the replication and for all quotations in `report/REPORT.md`.
- The equations (Eqs 1–9) were transcribed by hand into `code/repro_eq12.py` from the PDF, cross-checked against the pdftotext extraction.
